id: DRAFT-13617-colorized-logs-2.7-ohos-shell-nul-byte-command-substitution
category: ohos, portability, shell, testing
build_system: shell|cmake|ctest
phase: testing
match_keywords: NUL byte, null byte, command substitution, $(...), binary stream, ttyrec, ttyrec header, ansi2txt, ansi2html, ttyrec2ansi, pipetty, pipe I/O, OHOS, mksh, truncated output, File was truncated
error_signature: "File was truncated|ttyrec2ansi.*output.*missing tail byte|command substitution.*NUL byte|ttyrec.*header.*len field"
error_excerpt: "In OHOS shell test harnesses, capturing a tool's stdout with $(...) (command substitution) silently drops NUL bytes from binary streams: a ttyrec frame header containing \\x00 is corrupted, the replay output loses its tail bytes (e.g. expected 'hello tty' but got 'hello tt'), and stderr may report 'File was truncated'. The same byte sequence passed through a temp file is decoded correctly."
root_cause: "OHOS system shell (mksh) and bash both strip NUL bytes from the byte stream during $(...) command substitution (NUL cannot be represented in the result string), while the upstream testsuite writes binary inputs to temp files and compares output files with cmp. Any upstream test or consumer harness that round-trips binary data (ttyrec headers, termios sequences, escape payloads) through command substitution gets silently corrupted data."
rec_approach: "Always transport binary test data (headers with \\x00, escape sequences, ttyrec frames) via temp files (printf > file, then tool < file > outfile, compare with cmp/cat) instead of $(...) command substitution. This matches the upstream testsuite technique (stdin.$id / stdout.$id) and keeps NUL bytes intact. For pty-based tools (pipetty), also invoke the child through a script FILE (pipetty </dev/null sh script.sh) rather than `pipetty sh -c '...'`, which fails on OHOS mksh."
solution: "test_package/test.sh and test_ohos/run_ohos_test.sh in archives/c/colorized-logs/2.7 capture all binary-typed outputs into $TMPDIR temp files before comparing; ttyrec input uses a 9-byte payload matching the frame len field (\\t\\0\\0\\0 = 9 LE). Verified: upstream ctest 5/5 pass, test_package consumer checks all pass, test_ohos T1-T5 all pass."
fallback: "If a tool must be verified via pipeline, compare byte-exact outputs with cmp against an expected file instead of string equality."
prescan_pattern: "ttyrec|\\$(.*ansi2|command substitution"
verify_builds: "colorized-logs 2.7 (task r01 pc2-8): conan-verify G2 conan create ohos-aarch64 PASS, test_package consumer verification PASS, test_ohos 5/5 PASS"
severity: 2
last_updated: 2026-09-23
